The scanout's format modifier for the host (2026-11-05, research extension): a host that cannot read a guest
buffer's layout from the buffer itself copies every frame - an Intel GPU keeps no layout in the buffer, unlike
amdgpu's metadata, so QEMU refused even linear guest buffers on the Arc Pro B50 ("layout unknown") and copied
each 4K frame. When the host offers VIRTIO_GPU_F_SCANOUT_MODIFIER_VGD (bit 23, ours: it decodes the word; our
QEMU's virtio-gpu-scanout-modifier patch), SET_SCANOUT_BLOB's padding word carries the framebuffer's modifier
when the compositor gave one (DRM_MODE_FB_MODIFIERS: without it the framebuffer says linear whatever its layout)
and it fits a compact form - bit 31 set, the vendor in bits 24-30, the low 24 bits below: linear and Intel's
layouts do (scanout_modifier=0: never). intel_scanout=1 adds Intel's Tile4 (Xe-HPG, Xe2) to the primary planes
besides linear, so that the compositor's buffers can stay tiled - only with the feature too: a host that does
not decode the word would take Tile4 buffers for linear ones. Without the feature both are off.
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
